# Build-context exclusions shared by EVERY root-context image in this
# repo: the Render image (./Dockerfile) and the Railway image
# (./Dockerfile.railway). Both builders read THIS one file, so it must
# stay safe for both images. (docker-compose uses ./backend as context
# and is unaffected by this file.)
#
# Only exclude what no image ever needs from the context:
#   .git            history — images build from the working tree
#   .env            secrets — never bake them into an image
#   **/node_modules each image installs its own, per its package-lock
#   **/dist         each image builds its own frontend bundle
#
# History: this file previously also excluded frontend/, docs/, seed/
# and parts of catalog-10000/ to shrink the Render build context. That
# broke the Railway build, which compiles the frontend from this same
# context (its COPY frontend/... found nothing). The Render Dockerfile
# COPYs explicit paths only, so including those directories again does
# NOT change the Render image — its upload context is just somewhat
# larger (frontend sources, docs, the full catalog-10000 folder).
.git
.env
**/.env
**/node_modules
**/dist
